    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>A sliding cart is a compact, visually unobtrusive interface element found in e-commerce platforms. Initially hidden or minimized, it smoothly slides into view upon user interaction, revealing the contents of the shopping cart or order. This design optimizes space and provides a seamless user experience while shopping.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Login to your WordPress dashboard and navigate to Plugins &gt; Add New</li>\n<li>Search for &#8220;Restropress &#8211; Sliding Cart&#8221;.</li>\n<li>Click install.</li>\n<li>Click activate.</li>\n<li>Once the plugin is installed then you can see RestroPress on the left navigation bar of WordPress Dashboard.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.2.4</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed: Rapdly ajax call issue</li>\n<li>Code cleanup</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.2.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed: security issues fixed</li>\n<li>Code cleanup</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed: Menu popup close issue on mobile view</li>\n<li>Added: Option added to enable/disable cart icon/bar for mobile view</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added: New UI design added</li>\n<li>Added: Item quantity option added on cart icon</li>\n<li>Fixed: Icon/Bar able to visible only on restropress pages</li>\n<li>Fixed: Ajax issue fixed for bar cart quantity</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed: Minor bug issue fixed </li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.2.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial version released</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
